====================================================================================================
1. SPEECH MODELS
====================================================================================================

Skald's speech models are made by the National Library of Norway (Nasjonalbiblioteket) and published
under the Apache License 2.0. Skald does not include or redistribute them: it downloads a model from
the National Library's own repository on Hugging Face when the user asks for it.

NB-Whisper Large
  By the National Library of Norway: a product of the NoSTram project led by Per Egil Kummervold,
  with Javier de la Rosa, Freddy Wetjen and Rolv-Arild Braaten as key contributors, completed with
  the support of NB AI-Lab under the direction of Svein Arne Brygfjeld. Trained further from
  OpenAI's Whisper large-v3.
  https://huggingface.co/NbAiLab/nb-whisper-large
  Apache License 2.0.
  Skald's default model. On first run Skald downloads the National Library's own ggml-model.bin from
  this repository, at a pinned revision whose SHA-256 it checks.

NB-ASR Bokfink (beta)
  By the NB-ASR project at the National Library of Norway, with the work of its data, infrastructure
  and evaluation teams, on the Qwen3-ASR architecture by Alibaba's Qwen team.
  https://huggingface.co/NbAiLab/nb-asr-qwen06b-bokfink02-beta
  Apache License 2.0.
  Listed in Skald's model choice. Skald runs it as a GGUF file, which the National Library does not
  publish, so it is not offered for download yet.

Nordlyd
  By the National Library of Norway.
  https://huggingface.co/NbAiLab/nordlyd-asr-qwen06B-nov26preview
  Apache License 2.0.
  Shown greyed in Skald's model choice until the National Library opens it to everyone.

The text of the Apache License 2.0 is in section 5.

====================================================================================================
2. TRANSCRIBE.CPP, GGML, WHISPER.CPP AND LLAMA.CPP
====================================================================================================

Skald transcribes with transcribe.cpp by handy-computer
(https://github.com/handy-computer/transcribe.cpp), compiled into the program from the
transcribe-cpp-sys crate with two patches of Skald's (third_party/transcribe-cpp-sys/SKALD.md).
transcribe.cpp computes with ggml (https://github.com/ggml-org/ggml), takes its FFT from whisper.cpp
(https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp) and its Unicode tables and pretokenizer from llama.cpp
(https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp), and carries miniz. On Windows ggml's backends are modules
beside skald.exe, and the Vulkan one is compiled with the Khronos Group's headers.

